rem Angular Bisector and Tangent 1
rem https://projecteuler.net/problem=296
rem Count the integer sided triangles
rem ABC with BC <= AC <= AB and
rem perimeter up to Limit for which BE
rem is an integer, E being where the
rem bisector of C meets the parallel to
rem the tangent at C through B

use numbers
use io
use cli

arg Limit integer = 100000

rem BE = a c / (a + b) with a = BC, b =
rem AC and c = AB. With g = gcd(a, b), a
rem = g p and b = g q, BE is an integer
rem when s = p + q divides c = t s. Then
rem c < a + b gives t < g, c >= b gives
rem t s >= g q, and the perimeter is s
rem (g + t). For each coprime p <= q and
rem t, the g from t + 1 to the smaller
rem of t s / q and Limit / s - t all
rem give a triangle.
Total = 0
for S in 2 to (Limit // 3)
  Room = Limit // S
  Top = (Room - 1) // 2
  Low = (S + Top) // (Top + 1)
  Ps = Low to (S // 2) array
  Ps = Ps filter (Ps gcd S equal 1)
  Qs = S - Ps
  for T in 1 to Top
    Total += ((T * Ps // Qs) min (Room - 2 * T)) sum
  end
end
Answer = Total
Answer print
